@startuml
title The Tweedledum / Tweedledee 2-cycle — why alternating keeps arithmetic native
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
}
skinparam ArrowColor #7A5BB5

component "Tweedledum\nE_p / F_p : y^2 = x^3 + 5\nbase field F_p, group order q" as DUM
component "Tweedledee\nE_q / F_q : y^2 = x^3 + 5\nbase field F_q, group order p" as DEE

DUM -down-> DEE : a proof over Tweedledum needs\nF_q arithmetic, which is\nTweedledee's base field
DEE -up-> DUM : a proof over Tweedledee needs\nF_p arithmetic, which is\nTweedledum's base field

note bottom of DUM
  odd recursion steps
end note

note bottom of DEE
  even recursion steps
end note

note right of DEE
  p and q are 255-bit primes
  no pairing required
  126-bit security after the
  order-3 endomorphism correction
  gcd(p-1, 5) = gcd(q-1, 5) = 1
  so the Rescue S-box x -> x^5 is a bijection
end note
@enduml
